    id: "brought-in", section: "site", title: "What came in",
    body: "Right after the import, a card over the 3D view lists what came in: the photo and its date, the ground's climb, the trees, paths and roads, water, buildings, fields and courts, and holes. Look around and Start designing are on it. What came in, folded under the site's facts on the Site step, stays after that. It has a row for each place the import got things from, with what you can do about it. The measured trees have Measure again and Remove. The areas and trees from the photo, the buildings traced from the air and the creeks, wetlands and buildings from the US maps each have Remove. The shapes from OpenStreetMap have Update and Remove.\n\nRemove only takes out what's still as it came. Anything you've changed by hand is yours, so it stays. Undo, in the message that follows, puts a removed group back.\n\nWhen something didn't come in, its row is amber and the fold's title gets a warning mark: No aerial survey covers this spot (Check again), Couldn't read the aerial survey (Try again), Couldn't reach OpenStreetMap (Try again), or Some map tiles were missing.",
